cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this research software, cite the repository revision and the
  specific protocol package or certificate used in your analysis.
title: "Minimal Protocol Witness: deterministic protocol reconciliation for conflicting model evaluations"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Aydiner
    given-names: Tugrap Turker
repository-code: "https://github.com/tugrapaydiner/mpw"
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0-research"
keywords:
  - AI evaluation
  - protocol reconciliation
  - model harness
  - counterfactual evaluation
  - reproducible research
  - WebMCP
abstract: >-
  Minimal Protocol Witness is a research prototype for representing finite
  evaluation-protocol differences, executing or consuming controlled hybrid
  configurations, and verifying every globally minimum exposed substitution
  sufficient to reproduce a target evaluation conclusion. Results are
  directional, descriptive, and conditional rather than automatically causal.
